# fpldrop project context

Personal CLI (`fpldrop`): fetch **Bruno Mars XI** (manager `4703066`), render a pitch PNG, optionally post to X. Full agent brief: `AGENTS.md`. Graphic/caption work: `.cursor/skills/fpl-team-graphic/SKILL.md`.

## Run (Git Bash)

```bash
.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m fpldrop preview
```

Default to preview / dry-run. Do not tweet unless the user asks. `preview` prints a dotted tweet + pitch and writes `output/gw{N}.preview.txt`.

Live posting works. A **$5** X API credit pack is loaded on [console.x.com](https://console.x.com). First successful tweet: GW1, 23 Aug 2026. `402` / `credits depleted` means top up credits — Premium/Grok does not count. OAuth 1.0a keys only.

## Code map

- `src/fpldrop/cli.py` — `publish` (UTF-8 stdout so caption emoji does not crash Windows)
- `src/fpldrop/fpl.py` — fetch + `TeamSnapshot.caption()`
- `src/fpldrop/render.py` — Playwright PNG
- `src/fpldrop/twitter.py` — OAuth 1.0a post
- `src/fpldrop/templates/team_card.html` — visual source of truth (kits, points plates, Points/Transfers pills)
- Preview: `output/gw{N}.png`, `output/gw{N}.json`, `output/gw{N}.preview.txt`
- Log: `logs/fpldrop.log`

## Must not

- Commit or paste `.env` / `FPL_ACCESS_TOKEN` / X keys
- Put URLs on the graphic or in the caption
- Change caption shape without updating `TeamSnapshot.caption()`
- Treat FPL `refresh_token` as a working login path
- Treat this as a multi-user product; keep diffs small
